    "summary": "Smokin' Wheel→Other One→Wharf Rat suite & fiery Althea at New Haven ’82",
    "review": "The September 23, 1982 show at Veterans Memorial Coliseum is a high‑energy snapshot of the early‑80s Dead. The second set rolls like a firestorm – the Wheel → Other One → Wharf Rat suite builds into an electrifying Althea and barrels out to a rollicking Johnny B. Goode, while the post‑drum “rhythm devils” segment lifts the whole night. Jerry is on fire, delivering razor‑sharp leads and strong vocals (especially on Althea), Phil’s bass finally breaks through the mix with solid low‑end punch, and Brent’s B3 organ provides a thick, soulful backbone throughout. Bob adds his signature slide work on Althea and powerful vocal moments on Greatest Story Ever Told. The audience tape captures the raw excitement of the first set (Throwing Stones, Little Red Rooster) but the soundboard recording shines with clarity, making this night a must‑listen for any Deadhead.",
